Invented by Johannes Gutenberg around 1440 in Mainz, Germany, the movable type printing press revolutionized the way information was disseminated, marking a pivotal transition from the medieval to the modern era. By mechanizing the process of printing, Gutenberg’s invention drastically reduced the cost and time required to produce books, making knowledge accessible to a broader audience beyond the clergy and elite. This technological breakthrough not only accelerated the spread of literacy but also fueled major
